1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,229
Your last video got two million views.

2
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:05,560
A hundred and forty thousand likes.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,090
Strangers know your name.

4
00:00:07,110 --> 00:00:09,710
Brands are in your DMs every single day.

5
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:11,900
And your bank account says…

6
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:13,800
two hundred and twelve dollars.

7
00:00:14,030 --> 00:00:15,240
That's not a glitch.

8
00:00:15,269 --> 00:00:17,589
That's the most common way to be an influencer.

9
00:00:17,759 --> 00:00:20,439
So today, we're starting you at zero followers

10
00:00:20,459 --> 00:00:22,989
and taking you all the way to ten million.

11
00:00:23,149 --> 00:00:25,259
At every level, you'll see exactly where

12
00:00:25,279 --> 00:00:27,050
the money comes from, and how much of it

13
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:28,259
you actually keep.

14
00:00:28,429 --> 00:00:30,359
And somewhere on this ladder is the level

15
00:00:30,379 --> 00:00:32,509
where an influencer actually starts making

16
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:34,769
a living. It's not the follower count you

17
00:00:34,789 --> 00:00:36,750
think it is. Let's find it.

18
00:00:40,804 --> 00:00:44,113
Level zero. You've got a phone, a free app,

19
00:00:44,134 --> 00:00:45,733
and zero followers.

20
00:00:45,753 --> 00:00:47,753
And before you've made a single cent, you've

21
00:00:47,774 --> 00:00:49,993
already spent ninety-five dollars on a ring

22
00:00:50,014 --> 00:00:52,814
light, a tripod and a tiny microphone.

23
00:00:53,084 --> 00:00:55,173
You post every day for a month.

24
00:00:55,234 --> 00:00:57,374
Your best video gets two hundred and thirty

25
00:00:57,394 --> 00:01:00,224
views. Most of them are your mom.

26
00:01:00,524 --> 00:01:02,734
Here's the first thing nobody tells you.

27
00:01:02,984 --> 00:01:05,534
At level zero, the platform is making money

28
00:01:05,554 --> 00:01:08,174
off you. Every video you post keeps people

29
00:01:08,194 --> 00:01:10,684
scrolling, and every scroll is an ad they

30
00:01:10,704 --> 00:01:13,093
can sell. You're working for free.

31
00:01:13,424 --> 00:01:14,734
And you're not alone.

32
00:01:14,793 --> 00:01:16,924
Millions of people are doing the exact same

33
00:01:16,944 --> 00:01:19,043
thing tonight, in the exact same bedroom

34
00:01:19,063 --> 00:01:21,493
lighting, hoping the same app picks them.

35
00:01:21,783 --> 00:01:23,584
Most of them quit right here.

36
00:01:23,623 --> 00:01:25,674
Not because they're bad, but because forty

37
00:01:25,694 --> 00:01:27,784
hours of work for two hundred views feels

38
00:01:27,804 --> 00:01:29,514
like shouting into a pillow.

39
00:01:29,704 --> 00:01:31,274
But you don't quit.

40
00:01:31,414 --> 00:01:34,234
And on day thirty-three, one video hits.

41
00:01:34,283 --> 00:01:36,904
Four hundred and eighty thousand views.

42
00:01:36,924 --> 00:01:39,214
Overnight. Your follower count jumps from

43
00:01:39,234 --> 00:01:41,543
forty-seven to a thousand and twelve.

44
00:01:42,871 --> 00:01:45,652
Level one. A thousand followers.

45
00:01:45,691 --> 00:01:47,962
And your first brand DM.

46
00:01:48,102 --> 00:01:49,512
"We love your vibe.

47
00:01:49,632 --> 00:01:51,001
Can we send you a free hoodie?

48
00:01:51,021 --> 00:01:52,001
Just tag us."

49
00:01:52,102 --> 00:01:54,072
Free stuff! You made it!

50
00:01:54,501 --> 00:01:56,662
Except that hoodie comes with two strings

51
00:01:56,682 --> 00:02:00,072
attached. String one: the Federal Trade Commission

52
00:02:00,091 --> 00:02:02,132
says that if a brand gives you anything of

53
00:02:02,152 --> 00:02:04,582
value, even a free product, and you post

54
00:02:04,602 --> 00:02:07,251
about it, you have to clearly disclose it.

55
00:02:07,371 --> 00:02:08,771
Not hidden in your bio.

56
00:02:08,792 --> 00:02:10,352
Not behind "More".

57
00:02:10,382 --> 00:02:11,991
Right there in the post.

58
00:02:12,281 --> 00:02:15,021
String two: in the U.S., stuff you get in

59
00:02:15,042 --> 00:02:17,251
exchange for promotion is generally treated

60
00:02:17,271 --> 00:02:19,602
as income, at what it would cost to buy.

61
00:02:19,752 --> 00:02:20,741
So that "Free"

62
00:02:20,762 --> 00:02:22,882
hoodie might show up on your tax bill.

63
00:02:23,151 --> 00:02:24,931
And there's a sneakier catch.

64
00:02:25,051 --> 00:02:27,081
Read the small print in that DM, and they

65
00:02:27,102 --> 00:02:29,491
want you to make a video, tag them, and let

66
00:02:29,512 --> 00:02:31,662
them use your video in their own ads.

67
00:02:31,741 --> 00:02:33,731
So a company gets a professional-looking

68
00:02:33,752 --> 00:02:36,312
ad, made by you, starring you…

69
00:02:36,472 --> 00:02:38,122
for the price of one hoodie.

70
00:02:38,352 --> 00:02:40,661
In the industry, that's called content usage

71
00:02:40,681 --> 00:02:42,761
rights, and later in your career, brands

72
00:02:42,781 --> 00:02:44,162
will pay extra for it.

73
00:02:44,252 --> 00:02:46,201
Right now, you're giving it away.

74
00:02:46,461 --> 00:02:48,682
At level one, you're not being paid.

75
00:02:48,742 --> 00:02:50,252
You're being paid in hoodies.

76
00:02:50,331 --> 00:02:52,252
And you can't pay rent in hoodies.

77
00:02:53,336 --> 00:02:56,366
Level two. Ten thousand followers.

78
00:02:56,476 --> 00:02:58,966
And this time, the DM has a number in it.

79
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:00,856
Brands call this tier "Nano"

80
00:03:00,876 --> 00:03:03,506
or "Micro," and typical rates run from about

81
00:03:03,526 --> 00:03:05,926
a hundred to a few hundred dollars a post.

82
00:03:06,086 --> 00:03:07,917
You charge two hundred and fifty.

83
00:03:08,766 --> 00:03:10,726
They say yes instantly.

84
00:03:10,866 --> 00:03:13,406
And that's your first lesson in negotiation:

85
00:03:13,536 --> 00:03:15,876
if a brand says yes in four seconds, you

86
00:03:15,896 --> 00:03:17,626
probably asked for too little.

87
00:03:17,866 --> 00:03:20,216
Next time, you make a one-page rate card,

88
00:03:20,236 --> 00:03:22,326
with your audience, your average views and

89
00:03:22,346 --> 00:03:24,736
your prices, like an actual business.

90
00:03:24,976 --> 00:03:27,286
Oh, and watch out for the other kind of DM

91
00:03:27,306 --> 00:03:28,776
that shows up at this level.

92
00:03:28,926 --> 00:03:31,106
"Congrats, you've been selected as a brand

93
00:03:31,126 --> 00:03:33,446
ambassador! Just pay forty-nine dollars for

94
00:03:33,466 --> 00:03:34,536
your starter kit."

95
00:03:34,757 --> 00:03:36,556
A real brand pays you.

96
00:03:36,746 --> 00:03:38,796
If a "brand" wants you to pay first, it's

97
00:03:38,816 --> 00:03:40,806
not a deal. It's a scam.

98
00:03:41,056 --> 00:03:43,446
Still, the GlowSip money is the first real

99
00:03:43,466 --> 00:03:45,526
money you've ever made from your phone.

100
00:03:45,736 --> 00:03:47,936
Then you discover affiliate links.

101
00:03:48,007 --> 00:03:50,166
You get a cut every time someone buys through

102
00:03:50,186 --> 00:03:52,716
your link. Somebody buys a forty-dollar water

103
00:03:52,736 --> 00:03:53,956
bottle through your link.

104
00:03:53,986 --> 00:03:55,246
Your commission is…

105
00:03:55,356 --> 00:03:56,646
a dollar twenty.

106
00:03:56,887 --> 00:03:59,216
Affiliate money is real, but at this size

107
00:03:59,236 --> 00:04:00,466
it's coffee money.

108
00:04:00,576 --> 00:04:03,016
To live off a dollar twenty, you'd need thousands

109
00:04:03,036 --> 00:04:04,137
of sales a month.

110
00:04:04,306 --> 00:04:06,976
So you go after the thing everybody wants:

111
00:04:07,036 --> 00:04:09,286
getting paid by the platform itself.

112
00:04:10,472 --> 00:04:13,032
Level three. You hit the platform's payout

113
00:04:13,052 --> 00:04:15,882
bar. On YouTube, the full partner program

114
00:04:15,902 --> 00:04:18,403
needs a thousand subscribers, plus either

115
00:04:18,423 --> 00:04:20,942
four thousand watch hours in a year or ten

116
00:04:20,962 --> 00:04:23,442
million Shorts views in ninety days.

117
00:04:23,733 --> 00:04:25,312
Then come the cuts.

118
00:04:25,522 --> 00:04:27,983
On regular videos, you keep fifty-five percent

119
00:04:28,002 --> 00:04:29,082
of the ad revenue.

120
00:04:29,262 --> 00:04:31,343
On Shorts, you keep forty-five percent of

121
00:04:31,362 --> 00:04:32,822
your share of the Shorts pool.

122
00:04:32,862 --> 00:04:34,492
The platform keeps the rest.

123
00:04:34,872 --> 00:04:37,242
Your first month of ad money: thirty-seven

124
00:04:37,262 --> 00:04:38,942
dollars and twelve cents.

125
00:04:39,192 --> 00:04:41,702
And the amount you get per view isn't fixed.

126
00:04:41,832 --> 00:04:44,163
Advertisers pay way more to show ads next

127
00:04:44,182 --> 00:04:45,802
to some topics than others.

128
00:04:46,002 --> 00:04:48,322
A video about investing or software can earn

129
00:04:48,342 --> 00:04:50,432
several times more per view than a video

130
00:04:50,452 --> 00:04:53,302
of you trying weird snacks, because the advertisers

131
00:04:53,322 --> 00:04:55,442
behind it are chasing customers worth more

132
00:04:55,462 --> 00:04:58,882
money. Same views, totally different paycheck.

133
00:04:59,702 --> 00:05:01,653
That's why so many creators suddenly start

134
00:05:01,673 --> 00:05:03,272
making videos about money.

135
00:05:03,522 --> 00:05:05,872
And here's the part that hurts: ad money

136
00:05:05,892 --> 00:05:08,522
is paid per view, not per follower.

137
00:05:08,723 --> 00:05:10,872
You can have a hundred thousand followers,

138
00:05:10,892 --> 00:05:13,112
but if this month's videos flop, this month's

139
00:05:13,132 --> 00:05:14,512
check flops with them.

140
00:05:14,942 --> 00:05:17,262
So you do what every creator does.

141
00:05:17,392 --> 00:05:18,502
You post more.

142
00:05:19,771 --> 00:05:23,242
Level four. Fifty thousand followers.

143
00:05:23,502 --> 00:05:25,232
On paper, you're growing.

144
00:05:25,542 --> 00:05:27,742
In real life, you're exhausted.

145
00:05:28,012 --> 00:05:30,212
You film in the morning, edit at night and

146
00:05:30,232 --> 00:05:31,992
reply to comments in between.

147
00:05:32,262 --> 00:05:34,482
You're posting every day, because the moment

148
00:05:34,502 --> 00:05:36,682
you stop, the algorithm stops showing you

149
00:05:36,701 --> 00:05:39,552
to people. And everywhere you look, someone

150
00:05:39,572 --> 00:05:40,922
else is doing better.

151
00:05:41,141 --> 00:05:42,992
Their numbers are bigger, their videos are

152
00:05:43,012 --> 00:05:45,851
cleaner, their apartment has a neon sign.

153
00:05:46,211 --> 00:05:48,042
So you buy a better camera.

154
00:05:48,201 --> 00:05:49,442
Then better lights.

155
00:05:49,552 --> 00:05:51,872
Then a second phone just for filming.

156
00:05:52,391 --> 00:05:55,512
Then one week, your views get cut in half.

157
00:05:55,721 --> 00:05:57,682
No warning. No email.

158
00:05:57,701 --> 00:06:01,042
No reason. Your income gets cut in half too.

159
00:06:01,132 --> 00:06:03,152
Because when your whole business is one app's

160
00:06:03,172 --> 00:06:05,771
algorithm, you don't really own a business.

161
00:06:05,802 --> 00:06:06,992
You're renting one.

162
00:06:07,362 --> 00:06:08,512
Remember that line.

163
00:06:08,731 --> 00:06:10,362
It comes back at level eight.

164
00:06:10,721 --> 00:06:11,740
Quick catch-up.

165
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:13,841
At zero, you pay to play.

166
00:06:13,941 --> 00:06:16,290
At a thousand, you're paid in free stuff.

167
00:06:16,451 --> 00:06:19,120
At ten thousand, your first real check.

168
00:06:19,290 --> 00:06:21,241
Then the platform pays you a little, and

169
00:06:21,261 --> 00:06:23,571
the algorithm can take it away anytime.

170
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:26,091
And now you're about to get famous.

171
00:06:26,151 --> 00:06:27,990
Which is where it gets weird.

172
00:06:28,954 --> 00:06:32,544
Level five. A hundred thousand followers.

173
00:06:32,594 --> 00:06:34,735
People recognize you at the grocery store.

174
00:06:34,754 --> 00:06:36,354
And the deals jump.

175
00:06:36,454 --> 00:06:38,535
Brands pay this tier thousands of dollars

176
00:06:38,555 --> 00:06:41,295
a post. Four thousand dollars for one minute

177
00:06:41,314 --> 00:06:43,084
of talking about an energy drink.

178
00:06:43,784 --> 00:06:45,064
You feel rich.

179
00:06:45,294 --> 00:06:47,144
But deals don't come every month.

180
00:06:47,375 --> 00:06:49,444
One month it's four thousand dollars, the

181
00:06:49,464 --> 00:06:51,154
next month it's zero.

182
00:06:51,404 --> 00:06:53,785
And brands often pay thirty, sixty, even

183
00:06:53,805 --> 00:06:55,724
ninety days after you post.

184
00:06:55,944 --> 00:06:57,735
And now there's a new pressure.

185
00:06:57,865 --> 00:07:00,354
Your audience expects you to look successful.

186
00:07:00,534 --> 00:07:02,535
The content that grows fastest at this level

187
00:07:02,555 --> 00:07:04,865
is the content that looks expensive: nice

188
00:07:04,884 --> 00:07:07,474
apartment, nice car, nice trips.

189
00:07:07,674 --> 00:07:09,594
So you rent the car for the shoot.

190
00:07:09,664 --> 00:07:11,134
You film the "day in my life"

191
00:07:11,154 --> 00:07:12,394
in a hotel lobby.

192
00:07:12,555 --> 00:07:14,545
You spend real money to look like you have

193
00:07:14,564 --> 00:07:16,665
money, because looking rich is what brings

194
00:07:16,685 --> 00:07:17,644
the next deal.

195
00:07:17,935 --> 00:07:20,485
This is why so many influencers look rich

196
00:07:20,504 --> 00:07:23,324
and aren't. A big survey of over five thousand

197
00:07:23,344 --> 00:07:25,365
creators this year found that sixty-seven

198
00:07:25,384 --> 00:07:27,504
percent earn less than ten thousand dollars

199
00:07:27,524 --> 00:07:29,605
a year, and just under five percent make

200
00:07:29,625 --> 00:07:31,074
more than a hundred thousand.

201
00:07:31,314 --> 00:07:32,845
And when your income looks like a heartbeat

202
00:07:32,865 --> 00:07:35,404
monitor, it's really easy to start "Pay in

203
00:07:35,424 --> 00:07:36,875
four"-ing your life.

204
00:07:37,105 --> 00:07:39,125
We did a whole video on how that ends.

205
00:07:40,218 --> 00:07:43,388
Level six. You can't do it all alone anymore.

206
00:07:43,408 --> 00:07:44,878
So you build a team.

207
00:07:45,057 --> 00:07:46,968
A manager who finds you deals and takes a

208
00:07:46,987 --> 00:07:49,398
cut. An editor so you can sleep.

209
00:07:50,008 --> 00:07:52,008
An accountant, because now there's a lot

210
00:07:52,028 --> 00:07:52,987
more to count.

211
00:07:53,208 --> 00:07:55,927
And then there's the cut nobody budgets for.

212
00:07:56,148 --> 00:07:58,238
In the U.S., when you work for yourself,

213
00:07:58,258 --> 00:08:00,918
you pay self-employment tax: fifteen point

214
00:08:00,937 --> 00:08:03,468
three percent on your profit, on top of regular

215
00:08:03,487 --> 00:08:05,828
income tax. There's no boss taking it out

216
00:08:05,848 --> 00:08:06,818
of your paycheck.

217
00:08:06,838 --> 00:08:08,158
You owe it yourself.

218
00:08:08,367 --> 00:08:10,307
So that eight-thousand-dollar deal?

219
00:08:10,408 --> 00:08:12,678
After everybody's cut, you might keep a little

220
00:08:12,698 --> 00:08:15,168
over half. And then you read the contracts

221
00:08:15,187 --> 00:08:17,068
properly for the first time.

222
00:08:17,237 --> 00:08:19,788
"Net sixty" means they'll pay you sixty days

223
00:08:19,807 --> 00:08:20,987
after you post.

224
00:08:21,128 --> 00:08:22,878
"Exclusivity, ninety days"

225
00:08:22,898 --> 00:08:24,928
means you can't work with any competing brand

226
00:08:24,948 --> 00:08:27,508
for three months, so one energy drink deal

227
00:08:27,528 --> 00:08:30,187
can quietly block every other drink brand.

228
00:08:30,388 --> 00:08:32,288
And twelve months of usage rights means they

229
00:08:32,307 --> 00:08:34,858
can run your face in their ads all year.

230
00:08:35,028 --> 00:08:37,177
This is exactly what a good manager earns

231
00:08:37,197 --> 00:08:39,398
their cut for: catching the lines that cost

232
00:08:39,418 --> 00:08:41,197
you more than the deal pays.

233
00:08:41,457 --> 00:08:43,018
Earned, and kept.

234
00:08:43,138 --> 00:08:44,778
They're never the same number.

235
00:08:44,858 --> 00:08:47,028
And the bigger you get, the more people stand

236
00:08:47,048 --> 00:08:48,048
between the two.

237
00:08:49,076 --> 00:08:52,476
Level seven. One million followers.

238
00:08:52,496 --> 00:08:54,567
The number everyone dreams about.

239
00:08:54,726 --> 00:08:57,187
At this level, the brand deals look completely

240
00:08:57,206 --> 00:08:59,767
different. Top-tier creators charge tens

241
00:08:59,787 --> 00:09:01,716
of thousands of dollars a post.

242
00:09:01,787 --> 00:09:04,657
And yes, now you can genuinely make a great

243
00:09:04,677 --> 00:09:07,596
living. In that same survey, most creators

244
00:09:07,616 --> 00:09:09,637
with over a million followers said they earn

245
00:09:09,657 --> 00:09:11,747
somewhere between fifty thousand and two

246
00:09:11,767 --> 00:09:13,856
hundred and fifty thousand dollars a year,

247
00:09:13,876 --> 00:09:15,667
or more. Good money.

248
00:09:15,787 --> 00:09:17,326
But notice what it's not.

249
00:09:17,547 --> 00:09:19,897
A million followers sounds like a millionaire.

250
00:09:19,986 --> 00:09:22,137
It's usually closer to a really well-paid

251
00:09:22,157 --> 00:09:25,866
job. And it's a job with one terrible rule.

252
00:09:26,086 --> 00:09:28,807
If you stop posting, you stop getting paid.

253
00:09:28,966 --> 00:09:30,007
No sick days.

254
00:09:30,027 --> 00:09:31,256
No vacation pay.

255
00:09:31,437 --> 00:09:33,606
The second you log off, the money logs off

256
00:09:33,626 --> 00:09:36,537
too. And there's a second risk at this size.

257
00:09:36,606 --> 00:09:39,397
One bad clip, one joke taken the wrong way,

258
00:09:39,417 --> 00:09:41,127
and brands can pause their deals with you

259
00:09:41,147 --> 00:09:44,437
overnight. At a million followers, your face

260
00:09:44,456 --> 00:09:45,586
is the business.

261
00:09:45,706 --> 00:09:47,947
So when something happens to your reputation,

262
00:09:47,966 --> 00:09:50,427
it happens to your whole income at once.

263
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:54,389
Level eight. And this is where the smartest

264
00:09:54,409 --> 00:09:56,029
creators change the game.

265
00:09:56,330 --> 00:09:58,310
Remember level four, where you were renting

266
00:09:58,330 --> 00:09:59,210
your audience?

267
00:09:59,450 --> 00:10:01,909
At level eight, you stop renting and start

268
00:10:01,929 --> 00:10:04,190
owning. Instead of selling other people's

269
00:10:04,210 --> 00:10:06,769
products for a fee, you sell your own.

270
00:10:06,990 --> 00:10:09,879
Your own merch, a course, a paid community,

271
00:10:09,899 --> 00:10:11,529
a product with your name on it.

272
00:10:11,710 --> 00:10:14,629
And you collect people's emails, so no algorithm

273
00:10:14,649 --> 00:10:16,220
can ever take them away.

274
00:10:16,429 --> 00:10:18,529
And look at how differently it behaves.

275
00:10:18,799 --> 00:10:20,769
A sponsored post pays once.

276
00:10:20,789 --> 00:10:22,759
It's done the moment it goes live.

277
00:10:23,019 --> 00:10:25,700
A product you own can keep selling for months.

278
00:10:25,830 --> 00:10:27,069
The work is the same.

279
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:29,139
The difference is who owns the thing being

280
00:10:29,159 --> 00:10:31,600
sold. It's also riskier.

281
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:33,779
You pay for the stock upfront, and if nobody

282
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:36,169
buys, the boxes sit in your kitchen.

283
00:10:36,460 --> 00:10:38,440
But it's the first time your income isn't

284
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:40,819
a favor from a brand or an algorithm.

285
00:10:40,950 --> 00:10:42,350
It's already happening.

286
00:10:42,710 --> 00:10:45,070
In one twenty twenty-six creator survey,

287
00:10:45,090 --> 00:10:47,420
product and merch sales plus affiliate income

288
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:49,720
made up about a fifth of creator income.

289
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:52,000
Creators are moving away from relying on

290
00:10:52,019 --> 00:10:53,559
one brand at a time.

291
00:10:53,830 --> 00:10:55,490
Remember the side hustle video?

292
00:10:55,590 --> 00:10:57,889
If everything stops when you stop, you don't

293
00:10:57,909 --> 00:11:00,179
own a business, you own a job.

294
00:11:00,569 --> 00:11:03,310
Level eight is the moment an influencer becomes

295
00:11:03,330 --> 00:11:04,360
a business.

296
00:11:05,437 --> 00:11:09,028
Level nine. Ten million followers.

297
00:11:09,237 --> 00:11:11,577
At this point, you're not really an influencer

298
00:11:11,597 --> 00:11:14,447
anymore. You're a media company with a face.

299
00:11:14,597 --> 00:11:17,358
You've got producers, lawyers, a whole department

300
00:11:17,378 --> 00:11:19,518
just for sponsorships, and products sitting

301
00:11:19,538 --> 00:11:20,758
in real stores.

302
00:11:21,067 --> 00:11:23,327
Forbes estimates that the fifty highest-paid

303
00:11:23,347 --> 00:11:26,148
creators earned over a billion dollars combined

304
00:11:26,168 --> 00:11:28,427
in a single year, and the top one brought

305
00:11:28,447 --> 00:11:30,827
in about three hundred million on his own.

306
00:11:31,077 --> 00:11:32,947
And look closely at that list.

307
00:11:33,128 --> 00:11:34,977
Many of the people at the top aren't living

308
00:11:34,997 --> 00:11:36,347
off ad money alone.

309
00:11:36,528 --> 00:11:39,857
They've built companies: snacks, games, clothing,

310
00:11:39,877 --> 00:11:41,268
production studios.

311
00:11:41,388 --> 00:11:43,127
The videos are the marketing.

312
00:11:43,227 --> 00:11:45,057
The businesses are the money.

313
00:11:45,418 --> 00:11:47,197
But that's fifty people.

314
00:11:47,258 --> 00:11:49,798
Out of tens of millions of creators.

315
00:11:51,135 --> 00:11:53,845
So, which level is the one where an influencer

316
00:11:53,865 --> 00:11:55,655
actually starts making a living?

317
00:11:55,825 --> 00:11:57,485
It's not a million followers.

318
00:11:57,595 --> 00:11:59,775
A million followers can still be one bad

319
00:11:59,795 --> 00:12:00,925
month from broke.

320
00:12:01,115 --> 00:12:03,885
The most dangerous level is a hundred thousand.

321
00:12:04,105 --> 00:12:05,495
You're famous enough to spend like you're

322
00:12:05,515 --> 00:12:08,485
rich, but your income is a heartbeat monitor.

323
00:12:08,715 --> 00:12:11,345
The real level-up is level eight, the moment

324
00:12:11,365 --> 00:12:12,615
you own something.

325
00:12:12,785 --> 00:12:15,405
A product, a list, a business that keeps

326
00:12:15,425 --> 00:12:17,075
paying when you stop posting.

327
00:12:17,225 --> 00:12:19,605
Because followers are borrowed, and the platform

328
00:12:19,625 --> 00:12:21,375
can take them back anytime.

329
00:12:21,555 --> 00:12:23,315
What you own, you keep.

330
00:12:23,555 --> 00:12:25,645
So if you're thinking of becoming a creator,

331
00:12:25,665 --> 00:12:28,225
don't ask, "How do I get a million followers?"

332
00:12:28,345 --> 00:12:30,875
Ask, "What will I own when I get there?"

333
00:12:31,115 --> 00:12:32,855
What level would you want to stop at?

334
00:12:32,895 --> 00:12:34,135
Tell me in the comments.

335
00:12:34,195 --> 00:12:36,615
And if this video earns a single cent, you'll

336
00:12:36,635 --> 00:12:38,335
know exactly where it went.

337
00:12:38,515 --> 00:12:40,585
And if you want to see how that famous-but-broke

